  "method": "100 * (1 - median(candidate wallSeconds) / median(baseline wallSeconds)); within each job alternate baseline/candidate then candidate/baseline. Warm-up jobs retained separately and excluded from primary estimates.",
  "limitations": [
    "Small sequential nonrandomized campaign; no formal confidence interval or established noise floor.",
    "Chrome uses fresh headless processes; the completed Safari and Firefox campaigns use ordinary visible pages/workers with possible browser process/cache reuse. Browser numbers are not an isolated engine comparison.",
    "Browser receipts establish pinned retired work, frame counts and console output. They do not contain frame-content hashes.",
    "Baseline and candidate use the same inline threshold and no-DWARF build policy. This comparison does not measure download/startup or isolate individual x4/x5 changes.",
    "Compilation was user-reported and observed during part of Chrome and was allowed to continue. Later compiler-count snapshots were zero, but concurrent work was not controlled or quantified. Safari is not assumed to have experienced the same interference. These observed timings on an in-use machine are not a clean causal estimate. Conditions are retained in conditions.json.",
    "Power snapshots and aggregate load/compiler counts do not establish sustained power, thermal state, total machine utilization or the interference affecting a particular arm."
  ]
